/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  volatileAcids01_acetic_formic -- the two simplest volatile carboxylic acids of a
  wine or a food stream, dissolved in water: pH of the acid alone, at half
  neutralisation and fully neutralised.

  WHAT THIS CASE IS.  A STRUCTURAL ILLUSTRATION of the two ionisation records
  that make the acetate and formate families whole (chemistry/HAc-formation.dat,
  chemistry/HFo-formation.dat -- the second written for this case, C372).  It is
  NOT validated against a measured pH: no work in hand prints a pH for these
  solutions, so the case carries no `anchor` rows and says so.  What it does hold
  is an internal consistency the reader can check by hand: at half
  neutralisation the pH lands on the pKa of the record (corrected by the Davies
  activity coefficients), and the acid alone gives the weak-acid pH.

  TARGET: pH and species distribution (HAc/Acetate, HFo/Formate) at 25 C,
  0.1 mol/kg total acid, Davies activity (I <= 0.1 mol/kg, inside its window).

  SOURCES OF THE CONSTANTS.
    acetic acid  pKa 4.756, dH -0.41 kJ/mol: Goldberg, Kishore & Lennen, J. Phys.
                 Chem. Ref. Data 31 (2002) 231 (the record's own citation).  The
                 NBS rows (Wagman et al. 1982, Table 23:C p. 2-93) reproduce it:
                 dfG(CH3COO-,ao) -369.31, dfG(CH3COOH,ao) -396.46 kJ/mol give
                 pKa 4.757 -- two independent routes agree to 0.001.
    formic acid  pKa 3.732, dH +0.12 kJ/mol (formation sense): DERIVED from the NBS
                 rows of Table 23:C p. 2-83 (see chemistry/HFo-formation.dat).
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

application   choupoProps;
description   "Acetic and formic acid, 0.1 mol/kg in water at 25 C: pH of the acid alone, at half neutralisation and as the sodium salt, on the ionisation records HAc-formation (Goldberg 2002) and HFo-formation (derived from NBS 1982). A structural illustration, not validated against a measured pH.";
verbosity     2;
